   if (rule.enum && !rule.enum.includes(input)) fail(path, 'must be an allowed value');
   ```
   Because of `if (new RegExp(rule.pattern).test(input)) return;`, any string matching `pattern` short-circuits out of `check()` and completely bypasses `minLength`, `maxLength`, and `enum` constraints on the same rule (for example, `validate('a', { type: 'string', pattern: '^[a-z]+$', minLength: 5 })` would falsely return `{ valid: true, errors: [] }`).

